{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>ואמרה האשה אמן</b> — that her belly shall swell, Amen; that her thigh shall collapse, Amen, if she was intimate with another man. And in the Targus Yerushalmi: Amen if I have become defiled, Amen if I am destined to become defiled. And our Rabbis interpreted: Amen from this man, Amen from another man. And further they interpreted: since oaths are stated in the Torah generally, and it specifies one of them, that the past is rolled onto it — is it not a ק״‎ו (all the more so)? If for a sotah, who was not previously demanded [to restore stolen property], the past is rolled onto her, for acts of theft that were previously demanded, is it not logical that the past should be rolled onto them."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:37.959336193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}